  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tripoli. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Tripoli (Tripoley) is a multi-phase card game combining Pay Cards, Poker, and a Michigan Rummy (Stops) phase. Players ante chips onto a board with labeled sections. Holders of specific Heart cards collect from those sections. Then a Poker round is played, followed by a Stops/Shedding phase. Descended from the 500-year-old German game Poch.',
    objective: 'Accumulate the most chips by winning stakes in the Pay Cards phase, the Poker phase, and the Michigan (Stops) phase; the player with the most chips when the game ends wins.',
    gameplay: "Phase 1: Pay Cards â€” Heart holders collect. Phase 2: Poker â€” Pick 5 from hand, bet/fold. Phase 3: Michigan Rummy â€” Play ascending sequences by suit; first out wins Kitty + chips per card left in opponents' hands.",
